  "text": "WEDNESDAY SEP 14 1949\nMAURE MERRYEN\nVISITORS FROM\nAUSTRALIA\nA DAY\nKeith Dunstan.\nThey\narrived by\nwere\nMr. and Mrs.\nBCPA airline early Saturday after-\nnoon and left at 10:30 that night for San Francisco en route to Van-\ncouver, B. C., and New York, Mr. Dunstan, Australia air force veteran\nof World War I. is a member of the news staff of the Melbourne\nHerald,\none\nof the commonwealth's chief\nnewspapers.\nHe is the son\nef\nWilliam Dunstan, general manager of the Herald and well known\nin\nHawaii from several visits.\nMr. and Mrs. Keith Dunstan were mar-\nried Sept. 5 and four days later were US-bound.\nHe will join the New\nYork bureau of the Melbourne Herald for two years or more. During\ntheir brief stay in Honolulu they were entertained by local newspaper\nfriends.-BCPA photo.\nSeptember 5 is\nchosen\nby\nthe\ndate\nMarie,\nonly\ndaugh-\nter of Mi and Mis C. H. Mc-\nNative\" Brish On.\nDownes\nAvenue.\nNorth\nand\nKeith.\nvounger son of Mr and Mrs W\nDunstan.\nof\nWallace\nAvenue.\nToorak,\nfor\ntheir\nwedding at\nthe hoorak\nPresbyter ian\nChurch.\nMarie\nwill\nhave\nKeith's sister, Mrs Peter McIn-\ntosh, as her matron of honor\nand Ann Cornwell bridesmaid\nAnn\ntrained\nMarie\nat\nHospital.\nRoval\nMelbourne\nSoon\nafter\ntheir\nmarriage the voung couple mill\nleave for America, where Keith\nwill take up an appointment in\nNew York.\nMARiE AND LANE @ MONTHS)\nFRANK BARToN m.m.\n8' FIEND AM SUARNCE\nONE OF THE FLEMINGTOM TERM\nAND A REAR FRIENA OF MINE\nLAYE\nMALOLM\nALAN\nOCTOBER 1952",
